# ARag INGEST-RUNNER image pointer — the object the runner reads at RUN time to
# decide which image to run. Uploaded to s3://<filings>/deploy/ingest.env by
# scripts/deploy_arag_ingest_image.py, which substitutes ${REGISTRY} (the
# in-account ECR host, derived from STS at upload time — which is why the real
# account id is not committed here).
#
# Ingest-runner only. The app tier's two compose images live in the sibling
# 42-arag/app/deploy.env; the two tiers bump on different cadences and are
# deliberately not bumped together.
#
# TO BUMP THE IMAGE: pass --tag (or edit the line below), re-run the script, then
# just run `sudo arag-ingest ...` on the host — the wrapper re-reads this object
# on every invocation. No Terraform, no reprovision, no restart.
#
# The tag MUST name a commit that actually contains the entrypoints the runbook
# calls (scripts/bootstrap_db.py, scripts/ddl/, scripts/rebuild_mvs.py). Tags are
# immutable and SHA-based (never :latest), so the tag is a reliable record of
# what ran — but nothing yet verifies the SHA predates the code, which is the gap
# CL #8 (CI -> ECR push) closes.
ARAG_INGEST_IMAGE=${REGISTRY}/genai-dev/arag-ingest:arm64-SETME
